  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Instrumental music by William Boyce, Luigi Boccherini, Johann Christian Bach, Charles Frederick Abel, John Christian Abel, and Felice Giardini. On ff. 2v-45v are twelve sonatas for two violins ; with a figured bass for the violoncello or harpsichord. "Dr. Boyce " [1747]. On ff. 46-83 are quartets for a flute and violin (or 2 violins), viola, and a bass, by J. C. Bach, C. F. Abel (AbelWV D19), and F. Giardini. On ff. 83-114v are six trios for a violin, tenor, and violoncello obbligato. "Boccherini" [published about 1780?]. On ff. 114v-191 are two sets of quartets for 2 violins, viola, and basso (violoncello), in score, by C[harles] Frederick] Abel, published between 1761 and 1777, as follows: Nos 1-6. Op. 8. ff. 114b-154; - nos 7-12. Op. 12. ff. 154v-191</subfield>
  </datafield>
